# Doc ownership — used by the pr-welcome-comment workflow to tell
# PR authors who to request review from.  Uses CODEOWNERS syntax
# (last matching rule wins). Patterns support a trailing `/` for a
# directory and `*` as a wildcard, nothing else.
#
# This file intentionally is NOT named CODEOWNERS so that GitHub
# does not auto-request reviewers.
#
# Bot-authored PRs get one reviewer per changed area: the first owner
# listed on the matching rule. Put the primary owner first.
#
# Opt-in auto-request: append a trailing # auto-request marker on
# any rule and the pr-welcome-comment workflow will call
# requestReviewers for the matching owners, in addition to posting
# the welcome comment. Two forms:
#   /path/ @a @b   # auto-request      -> request every owner
#   /path/ @a @b   # auto-request: @a  -> request only @a
#
# The scoped form must list a subset of the rule's owners; unknown
# users are ignored. The PR author is never auto-requested.
#
# Docs team: once anyone on this line is assigned, requested, or has
# reviewed a PR, pr-welcome-comment stops requesting reviewers on it.
# docs-team: @lnhsingh @npentrel @fjmorris @seanangio
#
# Writer areas (as of Oct 2026):
#   @npentrel   — OSS (LangChain, LangGraph, Deep Agents), integrations,
#                 Managed Deep Agents, Fleet
#   @fjmorris   — LangSmith Intelligence (Polly, Insights, Engine),
#                 Evaluations, observability, prompts, general LangSmith
#   @seanangio  — Deployments (Agent Server, Cloud, self-hosted, BYOC),
#                 LLM Gateway, Sandboxes, enterprise and governance
#   @lnhsingh   — Docs infrastructure, billing, anything unowned (default)

# Default owner for everything in the repo, including tooling
# (.github/, pipeline/, scripts/, Makefile).
*       @lnhsingh

